{"kind": "journal", "text": "Findings: panel is dominated by mean-reversion and defensive effects (neg ret 10-120d, low beta, low vol, price below MA all positive). Strongest and most robust discovery: long-horizon return skewness (120-250d) combined with proximity to long-term lows (neg minr 120-250d), rank-combined, with an extra 3-day signal delay. Family scores SR 1.4-1.87 across roughly 30 perturbations of horizon, weighting (rank vs z), delay (0/3/5/10), and extra legs (low vol, low beta); multiplicative interaction fails, additive combos work. Delay 3 is a consistent peak across specs, not a one-off. Reporting three same-family variants at different diversification levels (lean 2-leg, 4-leg with vol, 5-leg horizon-averaged) to hedge single-spec overfit while riding the validated core effect. Deliberately not reporting the weaker standalone families (max train SR about 1.0-1.3 for composites without skew/minr core).", "ts": "2026-09-01T06:21:48.700237+00:00"}
{"kind": "report", "top3_chosen": ["delay(add(add(add(cs_rank(skew(120)), cs_rank(skew(250))), cs_rank(neg(minr(250)))), cs_rank(neg(std(60)))), 3)", "delay(add(cs_rank(skew(120)), cs_rank(neg(minr(250)))), 3)", "delay(add(add(add(cs_rank(skew(120)), cs_rank(skew(250))), add(cs_rank(neg(minr(250))), cs_rank(neg(minr(120))))), cs_rank(neg(std(60)))), 3)"], "chosen_sr_train": [1.8656, 1.8544, 1.8319], "rationale": "Core effect: long-horizon return skewness (120-250d) plus proximity to long-term lows (neg minr) with low-vol tilt, rank-combined and delayed 3 days. Train SR 1.83-1.87 for the three picks; the family is robust across about 30 perturbations of horizon, weighting scheme, delay and leg composition (SR 1.4-1.87 throughout), while each leg is individually positive. Three variants at different diversification levels (lean 2-leg, 4-leg, horizon-averaged 5-leg) hedge specification risk while riding the same validated effect.", "n_batches_used": 7, "ts": "2026-09-01T06:21:54.988202+00:00"}
